rline("push(table([2300, W - 2300], ['Part', 'Copy and behaviour (verbatim)'], [['Top card (while personal choices are missing)'", "push(table([2300, W - 2300], ['Part', 'Copy and behaviour (verbatim)'], [['Top card', '\"' + TOP.b + '\" (or \"Everything your results need is chosen\") · \"' + TOP.p + '\"'], ['Cards', M.ASM_GRP.map(g => '\"' + g[1] + '\"').join(', ') + ', then \"' + M.T_GOV + '\" (collapsible details; \"Prices & growth\" opens first; \"Plan length\" opens when a required choice is jumped to)'], ['Prices & growth extras', 'The inflation chips (1.8) and \"Growth assumptions set\" (Standard / Cautious). Choosing a set fills pay rises, cash, investment and pension growth with its rates.'], ['Each input', 'Label + tag (\"Set by LifeMap\" / \"Your choice\" / \"Assumed: add yours\" / \"Not chosen yet\" for the four required choices); value box or chips; \"Back to LifeMap\\'s figure ({X})\" once changed; one guidance line (verbatim below).'], ['Plan length card', 'Retirement age (box, prefix \"age\", whole numbers, any age from your age + 1 to your plan-until age − 1, with a calm note below 60: see 7.15): \"' + M.RETIRE_HELP + ' Choose the age you want to plan for.\" Plan until age, and the partner\\'s retirement age when their income is counted.'], ['Budget check', 'When all three budget shares are chosen and do not total 100%: \"Your budget split adds up to {n}%. It should total 100%.\"'], ['Set by Government card', data.asm.law.dom.groups[0].law.rows.length + ' rows (below) and \"' + data.asm.law.dom.groups[0].law.note + '\"']], { size: 15 }));")
